ant, hot temper, weak leadership. She may want to ask for crew cooperation evidence for C or D. But per instruction, she should make a focused argumentative contribution, referencing discussion, using explicit facts, and state her vote.\n\nShe could say: I remain with B but note that we lack evidence on his memory issue impact and interpersonal remarks; also we have no data on A reliability, so cannot consider him. I propose we gather info on C's crew cooperation and D's stress resilience before final. But need to give a vote. She could vote for B still.\n\nThus: PUBLIC_MESSAGE: I agree with James and Emily that B remains provisional best, because we have clear evidence of reliability and stress handling, while other candidates have serious gaps (A lacks reliability evidence, C has communication issues, D has hot temper). I maintain vote for B, but request additional info on C's crew cooperation and D's stress resilience.\n\nMETADATA_JSON vote B.\n\nProceed."}
